# Global TypeScript

- Enable strict null checks and preserve strict compiler settings.
- Never use `any`; use `unknown` plus runtime narrowing at trust boundaries.
- Add explicit return types to exported functions.
- Prefer `const`, readonly data, pure functions, and discriminated unions.
- Prefer functions/modules over classes; use classes only for required lifecycle or framework integration.
- Model expected failures as typed results, not exceptions or sentinel values.
- Avoid non-null assertions and unchecked casts; prove or validate the type.
- Keep imports through package/module public entry points.
- Inject clocks, ID generators, and I/O capabilities.
- Use exhaustive `never` checks when switching over unions.
